# Wave W17-W (Mt. Apex — Central): spine stone — gallery stone with a deeper seam shadow: cool ashlar courses cut by two full shadow seams, the gallery’s depth drawn as darkness between the stones (design: the spine of Borea, a grand gallery; the bell-frame stands in the side dark — the dark is this wall’s register). Mt. Apex — Central’s own wall — split from South’s jamb-banded step stone by the seams and the cold (gallery depth vs doorway warmth) and from North’s frost-rimmed zenith stone by value entire.
